# Cooking in Russian: вари́ть, ре́зать
subtitle: "Cook from a Russian recipe and give one to a friend: карто́шка, я́йца, ма́сло, соль, and the commands свари́, наре́жь, доба́вь — but вари́ for twenty minutes."
tags: ["russian","russian cooking","russian food words","russian imperative","recipes"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/cooking","grammar/imperatives"]
thumb: "band \"Boil it, or KEEP boiling it?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Ordering in a Russian restaurant: принеси́те, пожа́луйста","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/74-russian-restaurant.cast"}

## Cooking in Russian: вари́ть, ре́зать
